WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.862
Record a failed challenge against its
original criterion

2
00:00:03.982 --> 00:00:06.603
and identify the affected requirement.

3
00:00:06.723 --> 00:00:10.654
Do not erase the failure because a second
attempt passes.

4
00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:13.782
Examine configuration, method, instrument

5
00:00:13.902 --> 00:00:17.281
and system explanations through the site
process.

6
00:00:17.401 --> 00:00:20.643
The investigation must distinguish
demonstrated

7
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:24.418
causes from plausible ideas that still
need evidence.

8
00:00:25.038 --> 00:00:28.831
A wrong parameter can affect more than the
failed test.

9
00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:31.779
Assess related functions, earlier results

10
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:33.925
and proposed next activities.

11
00:00:34.045 --> 00:00:39.218
Avoid assuming that the investigation ends
at the first obvious correction.

12
00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:43.269
Determine what remains reliable and what
needs additional

13
00:00:43.389 --> 00:00:47.871
verification, with the rationale recorded
for responsible review.

14
00:00:48.491 --> 00:00:53.043
After the authorized action, define what
will be repeated and why.

15
00:00:53.163 --> 00:00:58.336
A passing repeat demonstrates only the
conditions tested after that action.

16
00:00:58.456 --> 00:01:03.628
It does not erase the original failure or
validate every untested function.

17
00:01:03.748 --> 00:01:06.009
Reconcile the new configuration

18
00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:11.233
and the evidence needed to support closure
before making a recommendation.

19
00:01:11.853 --> 00:01:13.853
A criterion change is

20
00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:17.559
not simply an administrative way to close
a failure.

21
00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:20.260
It requires scientific justification

22
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.139
and the appropriate documented handling,

23
00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:27.052
including impact on the study and related
requirements.

24
00:01:27.172 --> 00:01:29.172
Show both the original result

25
00:01:29.292 --> 00:01:32.120
and the reasoning for any later decision.

26
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.723
Do not report an unchanged pass where the
basis actually changed.
